; rowsum_row_out_of_range: a row at the grid extent must raise.
;
; The grid is 1x3, so the only valid row is 0. Row 1 addresses no line of
; the grid: the Rust VM used to sum absent coefficients to 0 while
; xqvm_py raised, so this vector pins IndexOutOfBounds on both.
;
; The grid is deliberately not square, and the row is deliberately inside
; the column count, so this pins the extent that is actually addressed
; rather than merely rejecting a large number: a check against the column
; count would accept row 1 here, and against a square grid the two are
; indistinguishable.

PUSH 3
BQMX r0

PUSH 1           ; rows
PUSH 3           ; cols
RESIZE r0

PUSH 1           ; row == rows
ROWSUM r0
HALT
